{"id": "EUVD-2026-97057", "enisaUuid": "91d43669-c419-3f29-ae57-59466f88f820", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the editThirdAppConfig handler that allows any authenticated user to modify third-party application configurations. Low-privileged attackers can replace client id, client secret, agent id and corp id of DingTalk, WeCom or Feishu integrations to redirect directory synchronisation and messaging to attacker-controlled applications or break them.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T14:33:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T19:21:00", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_sys_thirdapp_edit_config_post.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/system/controller/ThirdAppController.java#L412-L438", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sys-thirdapp-editthirdappconfig"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108883", "GHSA-cc33-2w5g-wpvx"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "844f8516-a1fb-30aa-81cb-aa5473e6d1cf", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bbb0e538-22ef-307f-a77d-c3bbe3f6ea5d", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}